The icon outlines embedded in the product are not. They are derived from the
Lucide icon set (ISC, with a subset derived from Feather under MIT), and both
notices are reproduced in full in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt.

ISC and MIT both require their notice to travel with the binary. The build
copies THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt next to the executable on every build for that
reason, and CI fails if the copy stops happening. If you redistribute a build,
that file must go with it.

THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt is generated by design/gen-icons.ps1 from the icon
set's own LICENSE. Do not hand-write it, and regenerate it if the set is ever
replaced.

See design/ATTRIBUTION.md for the full record of what is borrowed, under which
licence, and the rules governing what may be brought into this project.
